 "_about": "Clubs, cantons and regions. A club's canton has two automatic sources: the town in its name (GeoNames list of Swiss places, optional geonamescache package) and the canton of its address in the federation's list of member clubs (clubs_swiss_athletics.json), which is sometimes the home of the contact person. When both agree the canton is shown as certain; when they differ, or only one exists, it is shown as 'to be verified' and the build log lists the case. 'verified': club name exactly as in Alabus -> canton, checked by hand (a checked list, or a plain fact such as Biel-Benken lying in BL): it settles the matter. 'clubs' helps the guess where the name has no town: club -> canton, [canton, town] or [canton, town, lat, lon]. 'areas' maps words found in club names (regions, valleys, adjectives) to a canton. 'regions' are the three regions of the Swiss Athletics regional championships, as in the invitations given as sources.",
